{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310871,"nonce":"HLglaqWyhW/yj9DKg/O8kWclnX4=","title":"Phase 2 closed 2026-05-19 — TensorDemo on WASM works. Original \"arity mismatch in _start\" was caused by stale demo using outdated Tensor ...","message":"Resolved 2026-05-19. Both `SimdDemo.hx` and `TensorDemo.hx` now run cleanly via `rayzor run --wasm \u003cdemo\u003e.hx`.\n\n\n- **SimdDemo on WASM** — all f32x4 ops verified (arithmetic, dot, len, normalize, cross3, splat, sqrt).\n- **TensorDemo on WASM** — `ones`, `full`, `fromArray`, `add`, `sum`, `mean`, `dot`, `matmul`, `sqrt`, `get` all execute to completion.\n- **WGPU compute backend** initialises automatically on Metal/Vulkan/DX12 via wasmtime's wgpu integration.\n\n\n`TensorDemo.hx` was using a stale 2-arg API for `Tensor.ones(shape)` / `Tensor.full(shape, value)` / `Tensor.fromArray(arr)` and was passing `Int` indices to `get()` instead of `Array\u003cInt\u003e`. The current API:\n\n- `Tensor.ones(shape:Array\u003cInt\u003e, dtype:DType)`\n- `Tensor.full(shape:Array\u003cInt\u003e, value:Float, dtype:DType)`\n- `Tensor.fromArray(arr:Array\u003cFloat\u003e, dtype:DType)`\n- `get(indices:Array\u003cInt\u003e):Float`\n\nWhen the demo called `Tensor.full([2,3], 2.0)` (2 args), the compiler emitted a 2-arg call against a 3-arg signature — the wasm validator caught it as an arity mismatch in `_start`. Native happens to be more tolerant of the demo's bad-arity call (or just doesn't fail validation at the same point), which is why the bug looked WASM-specific.\n\nThe earlier diagnosis (\"the WASM emitter is declaring the IMPORT signature of `rayzor_tensor_ones` as 2-arg when the MIR extern has 3 args\") was **wrong** — the import signature is fine; the call site was emitting too few args because the source code was passing too few.\n\nFix: updated `examples/wasm-features/TensorDemo.hx` to match the current Tensor API. No `wasm_backend.rs` changes needed.\n\n\n\nNot exercised by any current demo. Will matter for Phase 4 (INT8 quantised matmul) when storage-side packed-int loads need WASM SIMD. WASM SIMD128 path in `compiler/src/codegen/wasm_backend.rs:2841+` handles `f32x4` only — `VectorSplat` / `VectorBinOp` / `VectorReduce` for non-f32x4 types fall through to `unreachable`. Add the missing `i8x16.splat`, `i16x8.add`, etc. when the time comes; same pattern as the f32x4 path.\n\n\nWhen `wasmtime` / `wasm2wat` report \"type mismatch in call: expected [i32, i32, f64] but got [i32, f64]\" against a stdlib extern import, **first check the source code call site arity** before chasing wasm_backend codegen. Native tolerates extra trailing-arg drops (or doesn't validate as strictly at the same offset), so WASM is often where the bug surfaces — but the root cause is upstream in the demo / call site.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `project_wasm_phase2` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}